in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @epistemologic

# @epistemologic/math/music — music theory as decidable mathematics.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-06, Reed + Alex → Mara, via
# docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md commit a8055f0): the substrate's agent
# coordination layer (@mirror/spectral) was reaching for established
# music-theoretic vocabulary — voice-leading, harmonic progression,
# cadence, dissonance, audition — because 2500 years of refinement on
# how multiple voices coordinate in real time already exists, and the
# objects are PRE-AI prior art whose decidability bounds match mirror's
# sub-Turing constraint exactly. Music IS the right intellectual ground
# for spectral coordination; this family declares the discipline.
#
# Load-bearing spec: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §5 (the proposed
# `@epistemologic/math/music/*` family, commit a8055f0).
#
# === Discipline ===
#
# A `@epistemologic/math/music` carrier IS:
#
#   - decidable: every object under this family resolves in finite
#     steps on finite carriers. Harmonic ratios are rationals; the
#     pitch-class group Z_12 is finite; voice-leading constraints are
#     bounded; counterpoint species are graded by integer index;
#     cadence types are a finite enumeration; dissonance is a curve
#     evaluable in O(1) per (ratio, partial-count) pair. The whole
#     family fits mirror's sub-Turing floor (per
#     docs/specs/mirror-compile-bootstrap.md) by construction.
#   - pre-AI prior art: Pythagoras to Helmholtz to Cohn. The vocabulary
#     is older than the substrate it now names. Substrate-pull pulls
#     toward what already has a name; this family is the realisation
#     of that pull at the math altitude.
#   - the audible register of the spectral triple: the parent altitude
#     (`@epistemologic/math`, implicit in boot/std/epistemologic/math/*
#     — `bundle.mirror`, `lawvere.mirror`, `spectral-triple.mirror`)
#     carries the (A, H, D) substrate, the bundle tower, and Lawvere's
#     fixed-point closure. Music is a fourth axis at this altitude: the
#     same spectral structure made AUDIBLE. Eigenvalue frequency IS the
#     harmonic the substrate is finding; voice-leading IS the morphism
#     vocabulary on the connection; cadence IS the closure event.
#
# === Species under this family (to land when consumers pull) ===
#
#   @epistemologic/math/music/harmonic     frequency ratios (3:2 fifth,
#                                          4:3 fourth, 5:4 third) as
#                                          fundamental constants; the
#                                          Pythagorean comma as a
#                                          holonomy measurement. The
#                                          number-theoretic substrate of
#                                          pitch.
#   @epistemologic/math/music/interval     Z_12 as a type; the circle of
#                                          fifths as the generator
#                                          ⟨7⟩ ∈ Z_12; the neo-Riemannian
#                                          transformations P, L, R as
#                                          group actions. The algebra of
#                                          pitch-class relationships.
#   @epistemologic/math/music/voice        voice-leading constraints as
#                                          types; stepwise motion as
#                                          default; leap as exception;
#                                          parallel fifths/octaves
#                                          forbidden. The local-morphism
#                                          discipline.
#   @epistemologic/math/music/counterpoint species counterpoint (1st
#                                          through 5th) as a graded
#                                          composition discipline; the
#                                          Fux ladder as a progression.
#                                          The multi-voice composition
#                                          rules.
#   @epistemologic/math/music/cadence      closure-of-progression types;
#                                          authentic (V→I), plagal (IV→I),
#                                          deceptive (V→vi), half (?→V).
#                                          The convergence criterion
#                                          vocabulary.
#   @epistemologic/math/music/dissonance   the holonomy-as-dissonance
#                                          map; Helmholtz dissonance
#                                          curve over frequency-ratio
#                                          space. The loss function at
#                                          the audible altitude.
#
# Forward-references only — sub-shards land as consumers pull them.
# `@mirror/spectral`'s sub-shards are the expected near-term consumers:
# `conductor` reads `cadence` (closure detection); `voice` references
# `interval` + `counterpoint` (algebra + composition); `audition` reads
# `harmonic` (frequency-ratio scoring). Naming the family root now lets
# those references resolve to named substrate instead of forward-promises
# against unnamed altitude.
#
# === Consumer relationship to @mirror/spectral ===
#
# `@epistemologic/math/music` is the SUBSTRATE; `@mirror/spectral` is
# the CONSUMER. Music grounds spectral, not the other way around — the
# mathematics existed long before the agent coordination layer it now
# names. The dependency points UP the altitude stack: spectral pulls
# from music; music does NOT depend on spectral. This family root MUST
# stay decoupled from `@mirror/*` so that mirror's coordination layer
# can be re-implemented atop the same substrate without circular
# pulls.
#
# === Parent altitude note ===
#
# `@epistemologic/math` is currently implicit — the boot std altitude
# carries `bundle.mirror`, `lawvere.mirror`, `spectral-triple.mirror`
# at that namespace without a declared family root. This family lands
# under the implicit parent; migrating `@epistemologic/math` itself
# from boot/std/ to a declared shards/ family root is a separate
# substrate-pull pass (to follow when a consumer pulls — per Last
# Responsible Moment).
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]: `prism
# @epistemologic/math/music { ... }` declares the family IS a prism.
# The five-operation block below is the canonical declaration form (cf.
# shards/mirror/spectral.mirror, shards/mirror/lens.mirror,
# shards/epistemologic/reality.mirror). Each sub-shard specialises
# from there.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §5 (the family proposal;
#               commit a8055f0; the load-bearing spec).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (the
#                      audible register of (A, H, D)).
# Related shards: mirror/spectral.mirror (the consumer; agent
#                 coordination layer reaches for this family),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/bundle.mirror (sibling
#                 at the parent altitude; the principal G-bundle),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/lawvere.mirror (sibling;
#                 autopoietic fixed-point closure),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/spectral-triple.mirror
#                 (sibling; Connes' (A, H, D)).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/math/music.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/math/music` as the family root; species live at
# `shards/epistemologic/math/music/<name>.mirror`.

prism @epistemologic/math/music {
  focus music
  project music
  split music
  shift music
  settle music
}

out @epistemologic/math/music
